# Kichele Link security hardening — review bundle

## Included
- `002_lock_down_rls.sql`: replacement draft for the local Supabase migration 002.

## Important safety notes
- This migration was written against the supplied live schema audit dated 2026-10-30.
- The live schema uses BIGINT identity IDs for gigs and applications. Do not rewrite migration 001.
- Do not reset the database.
- Do not run `supabase db push` or apply this migration to the live project yet.
- The SQL has been statically reviewed for consistency with the supplied schema, but it has NOT been executed against PostgreSQL/Supabase in this environment. It still needs testing against a disposable/local database before use.
- Keep real M-Pesa/STK payments disabled while the frontend and Edge Function are being changed to the mock-only workflow.

## What the migration changes
- Adds `applications.agreed_price` so each accepted worker can have a separate agreed amount.
- Adds `payment_transactions.application_id` to link a payment record to the accepted application.
- Backfills the new agreed price for existing accepted applications from the legacy gig-level price.
- Replaces broad RLS policies and direct table privileges with least-privilege access.
- Hides private profile phone/location fields behind authenticated profile RPCs.
- Adds atomic RPCs for accepting/rejecting applications, changing gig status, completing/cancelling gigs, and editing gigs.
- Removes the old payment trigger that forced transaction status to `pending` on every update.
- Prevents deleting gig/application/payment history through ordinary client access.

## Before applying
1. Verify the live schema still matches `supabase/audit/live_schema_20261030.sql`.
2. Run this migration on a disposable/local copy first.
3. Test all RPCs with two different authenticated test users (poster and worker).
4. Confirm the UI has been updated to use the RPCs and no longer writes protected columns directly.
5. Only then consider a reviewed production migration, with a current backup and explicit approval.
